            "More training for data enterers",
            "Validation is unnecessary for internal sheets",
            "Conditional formatting is decoration"
          ],
          "evidence": [],
          "hint": "A typo'd date breaks the monthly rollup \u2014 where should that typo have been caught?",
          "id": "da-validation",
          "mins": 4,
          "objectives": [
            "Data validation",
            "Error prevention"
          ],
          "prompt": "How do you make a shared input sheet trustworthy?",
          "situation": "A team expense tracker: typos in dates and categories break the summary; someone overwrote a formula.",
          "title": "The shared tracker",
          "why": "Prevent, don't fix: data validation dropdowns constrain categories, date validation constrains formats, conditional formatting flags outliers/duplicates visually, and sheet protection locks formula cells while leaving inputs editable. A shared sheet without validation is a data-quality incident waiting for a deadline."
