          "prompt": "How do you choose the chart type?",
          "situation": "A deck uses pie charts for trends, 3D bars for comparisons, and a table for a distribution.",
          "title": "The chart-type roulette",
          "why": "Match encoding to question: trends over time \u2192 line; categorical comparison \u2192 bar; two-variable relationship \u2192 scatter; distribution shape \u2192 histogram; part-of-whole (few parts) \u2192 stacked bar beats pie (angle judgment is weak; length judgment is strong). 3D distorts every encoding it touches. The chart is an argument \u2014 pick the one that makes the true pattern easiest to see."
