          "prompt": "How do you run the test properly?",
          "situation": "A button change shows +5% conversion after 3 days. The team wants to ship; nobody computed power or significance.",
          "title": "The 5% lift",
          "why": "Proper A/B: randomize, pre-register the primary metric and runtime, size for statistical power (enough users to detect a meaningful effect), then read significance at the end. Sins: peeking/stopping early (inflates false positives), tiny samples (noise), and multiple metrics without correction (one will 'win' by chance). +5% on 200 users is noise; on 200k it's signal. Do the math before shipping."
        },
