          "prompt": "Why might the 4.8/5 satisfaction score be misleading?",
          "situation": "A satisfaction survey (2% response rate) scores 4.8/5, but churn is rising and support tickets grow.",
          "title": "The 4.8 paradox",
          "why": "2% response = self-selected extremes; the indifferent middle (often the churners) doesn't answer. The score measures 'respondents', not 'users'. Fixes: random sampling with follow-up, compare respondent vs population characteristics, weight responses, and triangulate with behavioral data (tickets, churn). A biased sample doesn't improve with size \u2014 100k biased responses are still biased."
