          "title": "The buried lede",
          "why": "Pyramid principle: answer first ('We should do X'), then the 2-3 supporting reasons, then details as backup. Executives need the decision up front; they drill into evidence only where they doubt. Chronological 'here's what I did' structures serve the analyst's journey, not the reader's decision. Lead with the 'so what', earn the right to the 'how'."
        },
