          "prompt": "How do you present uncertain findings honestly?",
          "situation": "A forecast is presented as a single number. It's wrong; stakeholders stop trusting the team's numbers.",
          "title": "The false precision",
          "why": "Honest uncertainty: ranges instead of point estimates, key assumptions stated, sensitivity to drivers ('\u00b13 points if renewal rate moves 5%'), and pre-mortem ('what would change this conclusion'). False precision borrows trust and repays it with interest when wrong. Decision-makers can act on ranges; they can't act on a number nobody believes."
        },
        {
